(1. An automated intelligent system comprising: A computer-implemented system for controlling) Tj
T* (access to digital documents, comprising:<br>\(a\) an access request processing module) Tj
T* (configured to receive a request from a user to perform an operation on a digital) Tj
T* (document;<br>\(b\) an identity and permission verification module configured to determine an) Tj
T* (authentication status of the user and retrieve an applicable access permission associated with) Tj
T* (the digital document;<br>\(c\) a contextual data collection module configured to obtain one or) Tj
T* (more security-related parameters associated with the access request;<br>\(d\) a risk assessment) Tj
T* (engine configured to evaluate the one or more security-related parameters and generate a risk) Tj
T* (assessment result;<br>\(e\) an access control decision engine configured to determine an access) Tj
T* (action based on the risk assessment result and the applicable access permission; and<br>\(f\) a) Tj
T* (document access enforcement module configured to implement the access action by permitting,) Tj
T* (restricting, or denying the requested operation on the digital document.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2. An automated intelligent system comprising: The system as claimed in claim 1, wherein the) Tj
T* (security-related parameters comprise at least two of device information, authentication status,) Tj
T* (document access history, and access request frequency.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3. An automated intelligent system comprising: The system as claimed in claim 1, wherein the) Tj
T* (access control decision engine is configured to reassess access during an active document) Tj
T* (access session in response to a detected change in a security-related parameter.) Tj
